print("Although each of the worlds countries would like to dispute this fact, we French know the truth; the best food in the World is made in France. The best food in France is made in Paris, and the best food in Paris, some say, is made by Chef Auguste Gusteau.",end=" ")
print("Gusteaus restaurant is the toast of Paris, booked five months in advance, and his dazzling ascent to the top of Fine French Cuisine hasmade his competitors envious. He is the youngest Chef ever to achieve a five star rating. Chef Gusteaus cookbook “Anyone Can Cook!” hasclimbed to the top of the best-seller list. But not everyone celebrates its success.",end=" ")
print("Amusing title, Anyone Can Cook. Whats even more amusing is that Gusteau actually seems to believe it. I, on the other hand, take cooking seriously and no-- I dont think anyone can do it...",end=" ")
print("A light rain falls on a SMALL FARMHOUSE. The last remaining dead leaves tremble in the gusts. The quiet is shattered by a LOUD GUNSHOT that lights up the inside of the cottage. CAMERA pushes down and in toward a single window.",end = " ")
print("As we move closer, we begin to hear muffled SOUNDS OF STRUGGLE; furniture being bumped, dishes breaking, an indescribable CRASH, followed by an OLD LADYS SHRIEK.", end=" ")
print("We are close to the WINDOW now, when it is suddenly SHATTERED by a COOKBOOK. Instantly the action FREEZES.", end = " ")
print("Underneath its splayed pages, shielding himself from the shards of splintering glass is, inexplicably, a RAT", end =" ")
print("REMY. Hes scrawny, frightened, almost comic. Its hard notto feel sympathetic towards the little guy", end = " ")
print("This is me. I think its apparent I need to rethink my life a little bit. Whats my problem? First of all-", end = " ")
print("A SILHOUETTE darts out from behind a wooden barrel, pausing upright against a blood red sky. Mangy, sinister, the opposite of Remy. This is how most humans see RATS.", end = " ")
print("Im a rat. Which means life is hard", end = " ")
print("Assured the coast is clear, the SINISTER RAT scampers out into the yard, followed by DOZENS MORE RATS. The RATS move across the expanse of grass toward a COMPOST HEAP, which sits in the middle of a field under the darkening sky.", end = " ")
print("Resourceful and well coordinated, the rats grab bits of decomposing food and carry it off. REMY is among them, drearily going through garbage.", end = " ")
print("And secondly-- I have a highly developed sense of taste and smell", end = " ")
print("Suddenly he catches a SCENT; which leads him to uncover a nearly untouched piece of PASTRY, a discarded NAPOLEON.", end = " ")
print("Flour, eggs, sugar, vanilla bean, small twist of lemon...", end = " ")
print("The Napoleon suddenly erupts, and out pops Remys pudgy brother EMILE, covered in cream and completely oblivious to the destruction he’s wrought.", end = " ")
print("You can smell all that? Wow. You have a gift.", end = " ")
print("This is Emile. My brother. Hes easily impressed.", end = " ")
print("So you can smell ingredients. So what?", end = " ")